# -*- mode: org -*-
#+title: lumberjack

trying to write a text editor in c. possibly my first ever proper c software.

+ ~wlw.h~ is a bare minimum wayland client im working on right now
+ todo: vulkan loader
+ todo: rest of the editor

* goals
+ single tu builds (ideally ~cc main.c -o ~/.local/bin/editor && editor~ to run)
+ all configured right in source, no configs or runtimes
  + subgoal: keep it readable enough so you can orient yourself quickly
+ dont do useless work, when we know the system invariants, assume as much as we can
+ avoid external libraries where possible
  + exception: mesa vulkan drivers icds
  + avoid codegen (just complicates the build process and readability)
+ hardware accelerated where it makes sense
+ stall and block where it makes sense (proper idle when not focused, no background work)
